            <ArticleTitle>Transcatheter embolization of a bronchial side branch of the internal mammary artery for the treatment of a coronary steal phenomenon.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>289-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a 58-yr-old woman with unstable angina due to a coronary steal phenomenon down a bronchial side branch draining into the pulmonary circulation, 1 yr after coronary bypass grafting. The patient was cured of angina pectoris after microcoil embolization of the bronchial side branch.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
